# Technical Analysis

The vulnerability exists because the application creates a partially authenticated session immediately after successful username and password verification.

Instead of checking whether:

```text
2FA Status = Completed
```

before granting access to protected resources, the application only verifies that the user has successfully completed the first authentication step.

As a result:

```text
Username + Password
          ↓
      Session Created
          ↓
 Direct Access to Protected Pages
          ↓
      2FA Bypassed
```

This breaks the fundamental security model of multi-factor authentication.

